# Agent workflow

1. Read `AGENTS.md`. For phase work or safety/mutation changes also read
   `docs/AGENT_DEVELOPMENT.md` and the architecture status block in
   `docs/ARCHITECTURE_V1_IMPLEMENTATION.md`.
2. Prefer the matching `.cursor/skills/**` for this task
   (`execute-current-phase`, `repository-workflow`, `select-and-run-tests`,
   `spell-sync-ci`, etc.) — do not load every skill up front.
3. Inspect first: `python3 scripts/agent_context.py` (optional `--json`).
4. Implement **only** the current architecture phase (or the explicit fix scope).
5. Validate with local minimal: `python3 scripts/run_dev_loop.py` then `--commit-gate`.
   Run `python3 scripts/check_architecture.py --check` when boundaries change.
   Path-scoped ladder: rule `after-changes.mdc`.
6. Commit tracked changes locally as needed (any branch, no owner approval required)
   and verify clean trees at task boundaries.
7. Assess `python3 scripts/check_ci_necessity.py --purpose local --explain`.
   Do **not** run full CI when result is `commit-gate-sufficient`.
8. Run full CI (`scripts/ci.sh` + `check_ci_evidence.py`) only for publish/release or
   explicit owner “final”.
9. Read `CI_SUMMARY` / `CI_LOG` when full CI fails; fix without asking the owner to grep logs.
10. Update tests, docs, contracts, and ADRs together with code changes.
11. Do not claim pass without command evidence.
12. Capture baseline Git state for all three workspace repositories at task start.
13. Final task state: `git stash list` must be empty. Do not hide unfinished work in
    persistent Git stash between phases; use a named local branch with a normal WIP
    commit instead.
14. On modifying tasks: finalize workspace snapshot per `docs/AGENT_DEVELOPMENT.md`
    § Workspace snapshot, then report.
15. Do not advance to the next phase without owner approval (`advance-current-phase`).
16. Do not push, tag, release, or publish without explicit owner request.

